{'symbol': 'SPGI', 'date': '2021-11-09 17:12:00', 'title': "S&P GLOBAL RATINGS PROVIDES ALIGNED OPINION ON COLUMBUS METROPOLITAN HOUSING AUTHORITY'S SERIES 2021A, B REVENUE BONDS", 'text': "SAN FRANCISCO, NOV. 9, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ --\xa0(S&P GLOBAL RATINGS) S&P GLOBAL RATINGS TODAY SAID THAT COLUMBUS METROPOLITAN HOUSING AUTHORITY'S (CMHA'S) SERIES 2021A AND B REVENUE BONDS (SINCLAIR FAMILY APARTMENTS PROJECT) ALIGN WITH THE SOCIAL BOND PRINCIPLES (SBP). THE SECOND PARTY OPINION (SPO) IS AVAILABLE HERE."}{'symbol': 'SPGI', 'date': '2021-11-09 11:22:00', 'title': 'S&P DOW JONES INDICES AND THE LIMA STOCK EXCHANGE LAUNCH THE S&P/BVL PERU GENERAL ESG INDEX', 'text': 'LIMA, PERU, NOV. 9, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ --\xa0S&P DOW JONES INDICES ("S&P DJI"), THE WORLD\'S LEADING INDEX PROVIDER, AND THE LIMA STOCK EXCHANGE ("BVL), TODAY ANNOUNCED THE DEBUT OF THE S&P/BVL PERU GENERAL ESG INDEX, THE LATEST IN S&P DJI\'S GROWING FAMILY OF GLOBAL ESG INDICES BASED ON SOME OF THE WORLD\'S MOST HIGHLY-TRACKED REGIONAL AND COUNTRY-SPECIFIC BENCHMARKS. THE FIRST-OF-ITS-KIND INDEX FOR THE PERUVIAN MARKET USES RULES-BASED SELECTION CRITERIA USING RELEVANT ESG PRINCIPLES TO SELECT AND WEIGHT ITS CONSTITUENTS FROM THE S&P/BVL PERU GENERAL INDEX, PERU\'S HEADLINE STOCK INDEX.'}{'symbol': 'SPGI', 'date': '2021-11-09 07:00:00', 'title': "NEW S&P GLOBAL MARKET INTELLIGENCE INSURANCE INDUSTRY OUTLOOK PROJECTS THE STATUS QUO WON'T SUFFICE IN POST-PANDEMIC LANDSCAPE", 'text': "NEW YORK, NOV. 9, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ --\xa0INSURANCE COMPANIES WILL NEED TO ACCELERATE THE EVOLUTION OF EVERYTHING FROM DISTRIBUTION AND PRICING TO CUSTOMER AND INVESTOR RELATIONS, ACCORDING TO THE NEWLY RELEASED 2022 INSURANCE INDUSTRY OUTLOOK REPORT FROM S&P GLOBAL MARKET INTELLIGENCE. PUBLISHED BY S&P GLOBAL MARKET INTELLIGENCE'S FINANCIAL INSTITUTIONS RESEARCH TEAM, THE REPORT SPOTLIGHTS SEVERAL KEY THEMES FOR THE INSURANCE INDUSTRY THAT INCLUDE EMERGING PERILS, THE EVOLVING NATURE OF GLOBALIZATION, BALANCE SHEET RATIONALIZATION AND THE PERMEATION OF TECHNOLOGY IN ALL ASPECTS OF THE INSURANCE VALUE CHAIN."}